-- title:
--   Unique expansion g=sum_{i<p} aᵢᵖ tⁱ along t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying the predicate [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver K F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15), that is: every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ on the set of places of $F/K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $K$, proper in $F$, and principal ideal rings) with $D(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$; each place has residue field finite over $K$; and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Let $p$ be a prime, assume $K$ has characteristic $p$ and is perfect, let $x \in F$ be such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$, and let $t \in F$ satisfy $\mathrm{d}t \neq 0$ in $\Omega_{F/K}$. Then for every $g \in F$ there is exactly one family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,p \to F$ with $$g = \sum_{i<p} a_i^{\,p}\, t^{\,i}.$$
--
--   This is the statement that $1, t, \dots, t^{p-1}$ is a basis of $F$ over the subfield $F^p$ of $p$-th powers whenever $t$ is separating, the expansion underlying the Cartier operator in characteristic $p$. It is used in the study of the Cartier operator on a curve: the local analysis of regularity, simple poles and residues at a place under the Cartier laws, and the compatibility of the Cartier map with constant field extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_existsUnique_pDigits_of_D_ne_zero.lean

